{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098037-changing-targets-in-combat","id":1098037,"title":"Changing targets in combat.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-29T02:18:54-07:00","id":1098037,"title":"Changing targets in combat.","content":"Hello, first of all which VTM20 has an explained paragraph about switching targets in combat ? <br /> second, i had a little combat scene which i was very skeptical about how one of the players changed targets i'll explain below:<br /> <br /> matthew &gt; harrison &gt; john &gt; samuel <br /> <br /> Samuel has the highest initiative, john on second and so on.<br /> <br /> Matthew being the lowest initiative declares first, he declares attacking John.<br /> Harrison declares attacking John aswell.<br /> John simply defends.<br /> Samuel has no attacks on him, so he simply proceeds to attack to split his dice and attack both matthew and harrison once.<br /> Samuel rolls and resolves his attack.<br /> Once Samuel is done, Matthew and Harrison suddenly switch targets(roll willpower diff 6 and adding +1 to the difficulty) and attack samuel instead, samuel no longer has any actions neither can he switch his already performed action to defense, is this allowed ? kind of trumps the idea of having the highest initiative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T02:40:17-07:00","id":1098040,"title":"","content":"V20 doesn't have any rules for switching targets like that. The only rules that allow you to change an action once you've declared is to abort your action to defend yourself (spend 1 WP or roll WP diff 6, no +1 difficulty, fully described on page 274 of V20).<br /> <br /> The only book that allows any options beyond this in W20, which lets you change actions for a +1 difficulty. However this requires, &quot;drastic circumstances,&quot; meaning it is not meant to be cheesed such as changing your targets to a character that didn't declare any attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:11:59-07:00","id":1098070,"title":"","content":"Any other answers ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12206-onedayumay","name":"onedayumay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:51:46-07:00","id":1098197,"title":"","content":"Being able to switch to different actions in combat besides just switching to defense isn't something that I seem to remember you being able to do. It would completely undermine the declare first act last order of combat.<br /> <br /> What other answer do you want regarding this? Heavy Arms gave you the page number for the rules regarding aborting actions in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","user":"Kristviljan","date":". 05-29-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:07:49-07:00","id":1098235,"title":"","content":"There's a reason why they got rid of this in M20 and DAV20. What do you do when someone who is your target dies, like head clean off? Either you just let them change target, make them roll, or they lose a turn. I just make them roll Willpower using the abort roll and call it a day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:36:02-07:00","id":1098246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098037-changing-targets-in-combat?p=1098235#post1098235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a reason why they got rid of this in M20 and DAV20. What do you do when someone who is your target dies, like head clean off? Either you just let them change target, make them roll, or they lose a turn. I just make them roll Willpower using the abort roll and call it a day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd call that drastic circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T22:05:18-07:00","id":1098350,"title":"","content":"Nowadays, I just toss out the 'declare first, act last' mechanic. Characters act in their Initiative Order unless they decide to wait and gain a passive defense equal to (Dexterity plus Athletics/Combat Skill/2), rounded up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T03:05:52-07:00","id":1098717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1098037-changing-targets-in-combat?p=1098350#post1098350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowadays, I just toss out the 'declare first, act last' mechanic. Characters act in their Initiative Order unless they decide to wait and gain a passive defense equal to (Dexterity plus Athletics/Combat Skill/2), rounded up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean ((Dex+Ath)/2)?<br /> <br /> Otherwise an old but experienced fighter is not as good as a rookie even if the pool is the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T05:32:03-07:00","id":1098733,"title":"","content":"Yes, sorry about that, posted from a cell phone...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}